# Accessibility audit: Input (2026-11-15)

Scope: `spec/components/input/contract.json`, `src/components/input/*`, `src/mixins/native-control.ts`, `playwright/tests/input/*`. Standard: WCAG 2.2 AA and the native `textbox` / `searchbox` pattern (native `<input>` inside one shadow root with its label, description and error).

## Criteria

| POUR | Criterion | Result | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| P | 1.4.3 text contrast | Pass | `npm run check` T6 passes; probe: placeholder on input bg 4.74 light / 6.94 dark, label 19.80 / 18.97, description 4.74 / 7.66, error 4.77 / 7.04 |
| P | 1.4.11 control border | Pass | Probe: `input.border` on `input.bg` 4.74 light, 3.78 dark (1px); invalid border 4.77 light, 6.37 dark |
| P | 1.4.11 / 2.4.11 focus ring | Pass | Probe (Tab, `&globals=theme:dark` for dark): 3px ring plus border in ring color, 4.74 light, 6.94 dark against input bg and 4.74 / 7.66 against page; invalid focus keeps the destructive border (4.77 / 6.37) with a 20% ring |
| P | 1.4.1 color alone | Pass | Invalid is carried by `aria-invalid` and the error text, not only the red border; required by a text asterisk plus native `required` |
| P | forced-colors | Pass | Probe with `forced-colors: active`: border CanvasText `rgb(0,0,0)` 1px, text CanvasText on Canvas; focused input gets a solid 3px outline (the `focus-ring` mixin), box-shadow is dropped; disabled uses a GrayText-like color and stays visible |
| P | prefers-reduced-motion | Pass | Transitions wrapped in `a11y.respect-reduced-motion` (`Input.scss:46`) |
| P | 1.3.5 identify input purpose | Pass | `autocomplete` is passed to the inner input (`autocomplete="email"` read back from the shadow input) |
| O | 2.1.1 keyboard, 2.1.2 no trap | Pass | Tab reaches the inner input (`delegatesFocus`), typing is native, no trap; readonly stays focusable, disabled is skipped |
| O | 2.4.7 focus visible | Pass | Ring shown on keyboard focus in all enabled stories, light and dark; behavior spec covers it |
| O | Implicit submission | Pass | Probe: Enter with a valid value calls `form.requestSubmit()` once; Enter while composing (IME) does not submit; an empty required field blocks submission natively and fires `invalid`, which reveals the message; spec covers Enter submit |
| O | 2.5.8 target size | Pass | Input is 36px high and full width (probe `h` 36), above 24x24 |
| U | 3.3.2 labels or instructions, placeholder not the only label | Pass | `label` is required, rendered in a native `<label for>` in the same root, with a dev warning when empty; `placeholder` is an example only (contract note), and `hide-label` keeps the label as the name |
| U | 3.3.1 error identification and 4.1.3 status | Pass | `error` prop and native validity (shown only after blur or a submit attempt, never on first keystroke) fill `#error`, a persistent `aria-live="polite"` region; the input gets `aria-invalid="true"` and `aria-describedby="description error"`. AX tree: `invalid=true`, description equals the message. Native messages are specific (for example "Please include an '@' in the email address") and the story error says the fix |
| U | 3.3.2 required | Pass | AX tree `required=true`; asterisk is `aria-hidden` |
| U | 3.2.x predictable | Pass | No change of context on focus or input |
| R | 4.1.2 name, role, state | Pass | CDP `Accessibility.getFullAXTree`: `textbox "Email"` (searchbox for `type=search`); `disabled=true`, `readonly=true`, `required=true`, `invalid=true` in the matching stories |
| R | Description exposure | Pass | AX description is "We only use it for receipts." with a description, and the error text when invalid |
| R | ID references across shadow roots | Pass | `label for`, `aria-describedby` target ids all live in the same shadow root (`Input.ts:112-130`); an external `<label for>` is not relied on (contract Q) |
| R | Form association | Pass | Mixin `FormAssociated`; spec covers FormData, reset, disabled; `error` sets a custom validity that blocks submission |
| R | axe | Pass | Behavior spec: no violations |
| R | Behavior spec and `npm run check` | Pass | `tests/input/` 12/12 passed; all checks pass (A1 warn on spec/api.json is unrelated) |
| R | Screen-reader evidence | Pass | AX tree above plus the `__screen-reader__` snapshots (check S1) |

## Failures

None open.

### Notes (not failures)

- Parity open item (contract.json does not declare that `label`, `description` and `name` reflect): no accessibility effect. Name and description are computed from the shadow-root label and description elements, not from the host attributes, so reflection changes nothing in the accessibility tree. It is a contract-fidelity and Figma re-sync item only.
- `tests/input` also matches `tests/input-group`; one input-group test fails (`a slotted sb-textarea gets the shell ring`, `input-group.behavior.spec.ts:137`, box-shadow expectation). It is another component and unrelated to Input.
- `NativeControl.describedBy` and `renderDescription` are unused by Input (it renders its own `#description`); dead mixin code, no effect.

## Re-audit (2026-11-15, working tree after root fixes)

Changes covered: solid invalid focus ring, host `aria-invalid` marks the inner input invalid, synchronous render on `form.reset()` and restore.

- Invalid focus ring (`Input.scss:63-65`): With keyboard focus on the invalid story, `box-shadow` is a solid 3px ring in the invalid color: `rgb(231, 0, 11)` light (4.77 against page) and `rgb(255, 106, 91)` dark (7.04, `&globals=theme:dark`). At rest it is only the xs shadow, so focus is distinguishable from invalid at rest. Forced colors: solid 3px outline, shadow dropped.
- Host `aria-invalid="true"`: CDP AX tree shows `textbox "Email"` with `invalid=true`. The inner input gets `aria-invalid="true"`, and removing the host attribute clears it.
- Reset: right after `form.reset()` with no await, `FormData` is `a,init;b,`, the value is the default, and a required empty field has `validity.valueMissing=true`.
- Spec: `tests/input/ --workers=2` gives 14/14 passed, including the two new tests, with axe clean.
- Not re-run: `npm run check`, which fails D1 and D4 pending the Figma round.

## Verdict
Verdict: ready
